# REUSE 3.0 licence sidecar for a binary that cannot carry a comment.
#
# A font file has no comment syntax, so licensing invariant 8(c)'s "machine-readable, never a pasted
# paragraph" is satisfied the way the REUSE Specification 3.0 provides for exactly this case: a sibling
# <file>.license carrying the SPDX tags. scripts/gates/dependency-licences.php reads this file AND
# cross-checks it against the font's own OpenType name table (nameID 13), so a sidecar that disagrees
# with the binary it describes is a gate failure rather than a document nobody reads.
#
# OFL-1.1 is permitted for a vendored FONT ASSET only (CLAUDE.md invariant 8(a); developer ruling 2026-07-30). Vendored unmodified, so the Reserved Font Name clause is not engaged. Full text beside it as NotoSansArabic-LICENSE.txt.
